STATEMENT 3: InsertProductAsync
----------------------------------------
Original SQL Server Statement:
DECLARE @NewProductId INT;

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
    INSERT INTO Products (Name, Description, Price, StockQuantity)
    VALUES (@Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity);
    
    SET @NewProductId = SCOPE_IDENTITY();
    
    INSERT INTO ProductHistory (ProductId, Action, OldPrice, NewPrice, OldStock, NewStock, ActionDate)
    VALUES (@NewProductId, 'INSERT', NULL, @Price, NULL, @StockQuantity, GETDATE());
    
    UPDATE ProductStats
    SET 
        TotalProducts = TotalProducts + 1,
        AveragePrice = (AveragePrice * TotalProducts + @Price) / (TotalProducts + 1),
        LastUpdated = GETDATE()
    WHERE StatId = 1;
COMMIT;

SELECT @NewProductId;

DMS Error Output:
{
  "conversion_timestamp": "2026-02-11T11:04:52.645314",
  "status": "error",
  "error": "Metadata model creation failed: {'error': 'Unknown metadata model creation status: RECEIVED'}",
  "error_timestamp": "2026-02-11T11:04:57.206836"
}

Manual Conversion Applied: YES
Reasoning: Major changes required:
1. SCOPE_IDENTITY() replaced with RETURNING ProductId clause on INSERT
2. GETDATE() replaced with NOW()
3. Transaction syntax: BEGIN TRANSACTION -> BEGIN, COMMIT unchanged
4. Removed DECLARE and variable assignment - use RETURNING instead
5. Restructured to capture returned ID in application code

